  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Dynamics of Countering Human Trafficking in South Asia and the Indian Ocean 01-24</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The NESA Dynamics of Countering Human Trafficking in South Asia and Gulf Workshop is intended to build stronger relationships with security practitioners in South Asia and Gulf. The primary objective of the workshop is to promote dialogue and regional cooperation among security leaders in the region. The workshop is intended to broaden participants. understanding of local and regional civilian law enforcement strategies to deal with the threat of human trafficking through engagement with distinguished scholars, U.S. policy advisors, and U.S. defense personnel. Some of the results will be unique insights gained from these practitioners in the region, as well as the creation of a professional network of government, military, and academic leaders better prepared to engage in the international community. This counter-human trafficking workshop will focus on fully understanding the nature &amp; magnitude of human trafficking in the broader South Asia. It will be geared towards developing local capacity to counter this challenge and to study the dynamics that allow this menace to thrive at a global scale. Primarily, the workshop will focus on the creation, dissemination and use of standard operating procedures (SOPS) for victim identification and referral to rehabilitation services at the national and provincial level.</narrative>
  </description>
